//
// Three kinds of vector. An encoding pins the bytes, the byte order mark, what
// could not be held, three output styles, the same text in all fourteen
// charsets and the bytes read back in all fourteen. A decoding pins the
// format read (hex dumps, escapes, %XX, Base64), the charset used and why,
// the text, every replaced sequence with its offset, length and reason, and
// the same bytes in all fourteen charsets. A repair pins the candidates, their
// steps and the kind of evidence.
//
